<title>USA: VICAP sells $425 mln guaranteed snr notes.</title>
<headline>VICAP sells $425 mln guaranteed snr notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche debt deal was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager JP Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>The notes are guaranteed by Vitro SA and</p>
<p>was increased in size to $425 million from an original size of</p>
<p>$350 million.</p>
<p>Vitro SA is a major Mexican glass manufacturer, selling</p>
<p>products mainly in North America.</p>
<p>BORROWER VICAP</p>
<p>AMT $175 MLN	 COUPON 10.25 PCT  MATURITY 5/15/2002</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.650  FIRST PAY DATE 11/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BA3   YIELD 10.341 PCT  PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS    SPREAD +375/5YR   CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>AMT $250 MLN	 COUPON 11.375 PCT MATURITY 5/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.470  FIRST PAY DATE 11/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BA3   YIELD 11.465 PCT  PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS    SPREAD +475/10 YR CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
